Still EINVAL on tmpfs too. Hmm. Maybe my binary layout is wrong. VFS capability xattr format (vfs_cap_data):

```c
struct vfs_cap_data {
    __le32 magic_etc;
    struct {
        __le32 permitted;
        __le32 inheritable;
    } data[VFS_CAP_U32];  // VFS_CAP_U32 = 2 for v2
};
```

So layout is: magic, then for each of 2 words: permitted, inheritable. Effective is encoded in magic_etc bit (VFS_CAP_FLAGS_EFFECTIVE = 0x000001). So total 5 u32 = 20 bytes for v2. I packed 7 u32 (wrong order: I did magic, eff, perm, inh, eff_hi, perm_hi, inh_hi — wrong).

Correct v2: magic_etc (0x02000000 | effective_flag), perm_lo, inh_lo, perm_hi, inh_hi.

v3: same plus rootid (s32) = 24 bytes.

Let me retry with the right layout.

